  "director": {
    "note": "The pressure director. Each morning from day 2 the game measures the pressure on Anton, 0 to 1: how far Gilchrist suspects him (his surest belief that the lantern or the fire was Anton's), whether Anton's account has broken (his sister says otherwise, or he never gave one), and how many in town hold a true and damaging belief about him. Below the day's target, it promotes one incident latent in the night (press); well above it on days 2 and 3, one that gives relief (relieve); on a day in never_quiet it promotes one either way, trying the other kind if none of the first is left, and last a beat: the world going on, news and no evidence. One incident a morning, each once, chosen among those whose requires hold, in an order the seed shuffles. An incident only brings out what someone truly saw, or something true that happens that day: never a sighting nobody made. With active false it only measures (for a baseline sweep). An incident may also need Tamás's face to be still to come (memory_ahead), and may bring it forward (remember_now): the fever breaks early.",
